./.mpd/team/archive/rtl-dev/team.json:128:      "output": "ARCHITECT DESIGN (t2, read-only; grounded in t1 evidence + direct source verification of this repo).\n\n═══ §1 LSP SUPPORT FORM — FINAL: MIXED (Option A primary, Option B as documented escape hatch) ═══\nVerified facts this design rests on: (a) BUILTIN_SERVERS/LSP_INSTALL_HINTS live in vendored-upstream lsp-core/src/lsp/server-definitions.ts — NOT tracked in this repo (git ls-files=0); the only shipped artifact is packages/mpd-mcp-lsp/dist/cli.js (sha256-locked in VENDOR_LOCK.json, built by scripts/build-mcp.mjs from `MPD_UPSTREAM_ROOT`, upstream checkout present at /root/dshProj/oh-my-openagent). (b) daemon = lsp-daemon → @oh-my-opencode/lsp-core (package.json file:../lsp-core); the OTHER server-definitions copy (lsp-tools-mcp) is NOT built/shipped — irrelevant. (c) 31 builtin servers, ZERO HDL; language-mappings.ts has no .v/.sv; skills/lsp-setup/references has 18 dirs, none HDL; detect-lsp.ts filters by server.extensions → builtin additions auto-flow into it. (d) config-loader: project-config entries with non-builtin ids are silently DROPPED; user config honors custom command+extensions; precedence project>user>builtin then priority desc; user-config path = ~/.codex/lsp-client.json OR env LSP_TOOLS_MCP_USER_CONFIG (proxy.ts:147, single path). (e) Machine: iverilog+verilator PRESENT (oss-cad-suite); verible/slang/vcs absent; bun cache populated (1694 entries — lsp external deps js-yaml/jsonc-parser/zod likely present).\n\nOPTION A (PRIMARY — add BOTH as builtins, upstream untouched via in-repo overlay):\n- New files packages/mpd-mcp-lsp/overlay/lsp/{server-definitions.ts, language-mappings.ts} = patched copies. server-definitions: two BUILTIN_SERVERS entries — id \"verible\": command [\"verible-verilog-ls\"], extensions [\".v\",\".vh\"], LSP_INSTALL_HINTS verible → \"download prebuilt binaries: https://github.com/chipsalliance/verible/releases\"; id \"slang-server\": command [\"slang-server\"], extensions [\".sv\",\".svh\"], LSP_INSTALL_HINTS slang-server → \"per-platform static binaries: https://github.com/hudson-trading/slang-server/releases\". language-mappings: EXT_TO_LANG += \".v\"/\".vh\"→\"verilog\", \".sv\"/\".svh\"→\"systemverilog\". No overlap between the two servers' extensions (clean resolution).\n- scripts/build-mcp.mjs: after cpSync(lsp-core) apply overlay copies; add DRIFT GUARD — an anchor marker (e.g. `const BUILTIN_BUILD_ANCHOR = \"mpd-rtl-overlay-v1\"`) must exist in both source and overlay or build FAILS loudly (prevents silent upstream drift).\n- Rebuild: `MPD_UPSTREAM_ROOT=/root/dshProj/oh-my-openagent node scripts/build-mcp.mjs` → new dist/cli.js; re-lock its sha256 in VENDOR_LOCK.json; run scripts/verify-vendor.mjs.\n- lsp-setup skill: new references/verilog/README.md + references/systemverilog/README.md mirroring the c-cpp/README.md skeleton (builtin/command/extensions/install hint/install/configure/limitations/troubleshooting/verify) + SKILL.md routing rows (.v/.vh→verilog, .sv/.svh→systemverilog) + description update. EN-only — matches all 18 existing reference dirs (AGENTS.md bilingual mandate covers README/docs/packages READMEs; skill corpus is agent-facing English-only; bilingual user coverage lives in docs/rtl-verif-guide*.md at t9). Content notes to include: verible — hover experimental (do NOT enable in builtin command; mention --lsp_enable_hover), project-wide def/refs need verible.filelist, rules in .rules.verible_lint; slang-server — real slang shallow-compilation diagnostics on keystroke, .slang/server.json hierarchical config (workspace→user→local, flags/index/build/wcpCommand), known limits (untaken ifdef branches, --single-unit unsupported, some UVM class-in-package patterns).\n- Diff: 2 overlay files (~80 lines), build-mcp +~15 lines (guard), 2 ref docs (~60 lines each), SKILL.md +5 rows, VENDOR_LOCK 1 sha, rebuilt dist. Effort: Short (~2-4 h incl. QA).\n\nOPTION B (escape hatch; DELIBERATELY NOT the primary form): ship packages/mpd-mcp-lsp/templates/rtl-lsp-client.json (example user-config with custom verible/slang commands for hand-built binaries) + docs telling the user to merge/copy into ~/.codex/lsp-client.json. DO NOT auto-pin LSP_TOOLS_MCP_USER_CONFIG on the mcp-lsp row: the loader takes ONE user-config path, so pinning would shadow a user's existing Codex/OpenCode LSP config. B alone cannot give out-of-the-box HDL auto-resolution nor the builtin install-hint UX — hence A primary.\n\nDECISION POINTS DP-1..DP-11 at bottom (DP-1=this choice).\n\n═══ §2 mpd-verif PLUGIN DESIGN ═══\nPackage packages/mpd-verif-plugin (@mpd-dsh/verif; new bundle row). Zero runtime deps; tools via ctx.tools.register (pattern: packages/mpd-codegraph-plugin/src/index.ts); spawnSync argv arrays (never shell-string concat); workspace state ONLY under <cwd>/.mpd/verif/ (work dir) + <cwd>/.venv-rtl (venv) — AGENTS.md §6 compliant, never ~/.dsh.\nEnv resolution (MPD_DSH_* wins, PATH fallback): MPD_DSH_VERIF_IVERILOG | MPD_DSH_VERIF_VERILATOR | MPD_DSH_VERIF_VCS | MPD_DSH_VERIF_VENV | MPD_DSH_VERIF_WORK. VCS lane inherits parent env untouched (VCS_HOME/LM_LICENSE_FILE/SNPSLMD_LICENSE_FILE/PATH).\n\nTOOLS (6):\n1. mpd_verif_venv — {action: status|create|info (default status), path?}. create: `python3 -m venv` bootstrap is the ONLY sanctioned use of system python, then `<venv>/bin/pip install \"cocotb>=2.0\"` — NO system pip/pipx/--user/--system ever. status output: {ok, venv, python, cocotbVersion?, verdict: ok|missing|setup-required, message} (message = actionable exact commands when missing-ready).\n2. mpd_verif_backends — {backend: iverilog|verilator|vcs|all}. Output per backend: {binary (effective env/PATH), present, version, licenseHint? (vcs env checklist)}. This tool IS the auto-detect surface and the QA probe.\n3. mpd_verif_compile — {backend, sources[], top?, includes?, defines?, target: lint|compile (default lint)}. Lint-only P0: iverilog `-g2012 -tnull -Wall`, verilator `--lint-only -Wall`, vcs `-lca -sverilog +lint=all -f <gen filelist>`; output {ok, exitCode, diagnostics[] {file,line,code,severity,message} best-effort parsed, logPath}. No python/cocotb involved.\n4. mpd_verif_sim — cocotb lane, iverilog|verilator ONLY. {backend, top, tbModules? (default [top+\"_tb\"]), sources[], includes?, defines?, testFilter?, seed?, waves (default true), timeoutSec}. Flow: (1) IRON GATE — venv exists + `<venv>/bin/python -c 'import cocotb'` passes, else REFUSE VERIF_E_NO_VENV with exact setup command; (2) backend resolve; (3) generate <work>/<case>/runner.py using cocotb.runner API (cocotb>=2.0 pinned; older → VERIF_E_UNSUPPORTED with version message); (4) exec ONLY `<venv>/bin/python runner.py` (never bare python) → results.xml; (5) parse results.xml → per-case status. waves=true emits FST: verilator build_args --trace --trace-fst --trace-structs; icarus -fst (implementer verifies exact flag catalog in t4/t7). Output: {ok, backend, top, seed, cases[] {name,status:pass|fail|error|skip,timeMs,failureMsg?}, resultsXml, simLog, waves[] {file,fmt}}.\n5. mpd_verif_uvm — VCS-only UVM lane. {action: compile|run|regress|wave|merge-cov|clean, top, filelist, includes?, defines?, test?, uvmVer: \"1.2\", seed?, coverage, waveFmt: fsdb|vcd, verbosity}. Gates: VCS absent → VERIF_E_NO_BACKEND (license hints); missing VERDI_HOME/NOVAS_HOME/VCS_HOME when wave/coverage requested → VERIF_E_ENV checklist. Command contract mirrors the gen-tb-skill makefile contract (UVM_VER=1.2; seed default date+%N; per-case work/work_<case>_ dirs; -cm line+cond+tgl + urg merge for cov; $fsdbDumpfile for waves). Template-layout contract (validated before compile; missing → VERIF_E_TEMPLATE listing expected files): tree <ip>/{rtl,script,tb,top,test,work/}, tb_api_primitives.svh single-BFM source-of-truth, *_test naming, mandatory sanity_test + reg_access_test. Methodology grounded in gen-tb-skill (STRUCTURE) + raysalemi/uvmprimer (METHODOLOGY patterns: env/agent/sequence/config-db/scoreboard/covergroup layering) — methodology reference only, NO code reuse (license discipline). vcs-verdi-developer = reference-only, NON-GOLDEN (owner unvalidated), used solely to cross-check CLI forms in docs; never asserted by QA.\n6. mpd_verif_regress — {backend, cases[]/glob, seedBase?, maxFailures?, stopOnError?}. Per-case work dirs; seed per case derived deterministically from seedBase+idx (default seedBase=date+1%N per gen-tb); aggregates results.xml (cocotb lane) or UVM regress logs; writes <work>/results.json + markdown report. Output: {ok, total, passed, failed, seedBase, cases[] {backend,test,seed,status,timeMs,wave?}, reportMarkdown}.\n\nBACKEND ABSTRACTION (internal): {id, resolve()→{binary, present, version}, lintArgs(ctx), simArgs(ctx), compileArgs(ctx)}. Registry {iverilog, verilator, vcs}. Nothing fancier — three concrete configs, one runner core.\n\nERROR TAXONOMY (all refusals = {code, message: 1-line cause, hint: exact remediation}): VERIF_E_NO_BACKEND · VERIF_E_NO_VENV · VERIF_E_COCOTB_ABSENT · VERIF_E_UNSUPPORTED · VERIF_E_LICENSE · VERIF_E_ENV · VERIF_E_COMPILE · VERIF_E_RUN · VERIF_E_TIMEOUT · VERIF_E_TEMPLATE.\n\nDecoupling note: plugin ships ZERO template content; rich cocotb/UVM skeletons live in skills/rtl-verif (t5). mpd_verif_uvm only validates+orchestrates layout someone scaffolded — no path coupling between plugin and skill dir.\n\n═══ §3 COCOTB VENV IRON RULE (verbatim contract for implementers/QA) ═══\n1) Venv = <workspace>/.venv-rtl, or MPD_DSH_VERIF_VENV. 2) Creation ONLY via `python3 -m venv` (the single legal use of the system interpreter). 3) EVERY pip install = `<venv>/bin/pip`. 4) EVERY cocotb execution = `<venv>/bin/python runner.py`. 5) NEVER: system pip, pipx for cocotb, --user, --system, --system-site-packages (venv created fully isolated). 6) mpd_verif_sim REFUSES (VERIF_E_NO_VENV) unless venv exists AND cocotb imports inside it; refusal message carries `python3 -m venv .venv-rtl && .venv-rtl/bin/pip install \"cocotb>=2.0\"` plus `mpd_verif_venv(action:\"create\")`. 7) Venv is workspace-local only (never ~/.dsh, never global). 8) QA ACCEPTANCE (t7, mandatory): after any sim run, system python still must NOT import cocotb (proves zero global pollution); all writes land under workspace/.venv-rtl + .mpd/verif.\n\n═══ §4 UVM ENGINES GATING ═══\n- mpd_verif_uvm: VCS-backed ONLY (no backend parameter — fixed vcs). iverilog/verilator + any UVM request → VERIF_E_UNSUPPORTED (hard refusal, not warning) with rationale (owner decision: cocotb for OSS backends; UVM exclusively the VCS methodology lane).\n- mpd_verif_sim: vcs → VERIF_E_UNSUPPORTED pointing to mpd_verif_uvm. (cocotb-on-VCS deliberately NOT offered even though cocotb technically supports it — owner scope says cocotb for Icarus/Verilator.)\n- Methodology double-grounding: gen-tb-skill = structure (7-phase pipeline → plugin's capped compile-fix loop (default 3 attempts) writing <work>/unresolved.md on exhaustion; fixed generated tree; tb_api_primitives.svh shared BFM; UVM_VER=1.2 makefile contract) + raysalemi/uvmprimer = teaching order for scaffold docs (env→agent→sequence layering, config_db, scoreboard, covergroup, register model).\n\n═══ §5 WAVEFORM MCP WIRING (t9 does the rows; spec here) ═══\nTwo NEW @deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client rows in cordis.patch.yml (pattern = existing astgrep/lsp rows):\n- id mcp-wave-mcp: serverName wave_mcp, stdio. command: `!!js process.env.MPD_DSH_WAVE_MCP_BIN || \"wave-mcp\"`. args: `!!js [\"--session\", process.env.MPD_DSH_WAVE_MCP_SESSION || (process.env.DSH_HOME ? process.env.DSH_HOME + \"/wave-mcp\" : \".wave-mcp\")]` (exact base evaluation t9 verifies at boot). toolCallTimeoutMs 120000 (FST loads). Lane: cocotb/OSS FST (verilator/icarus --trace-fst). Py 3.10–3.13, glibc>=2.28, MCP SDK v2.\n- id mcp-traceweave: serverName traceweave, stdio. command: `!!js process.env.MPD_DSH_TRACEWEAVE_BIN || \"traceweave-mcp\"`, args [], env {} (EDA env inherited from dsh parent; docs instruct exporting VERDI_HOME/NOVAS_HOME/VCS_HOME+license vars in the launching shell). toolCallTimeoutMs 120000. Lane: VCS/UVM VCD/FSDB+logs. Py 3.11+, mcp==1.27.0.\n- INSTALL POLICY (docs, no vendoring): wave-mcp → dedicated tool venv (`python3 -m venv ~/.venvs/wave-mcp && ~/.venvs/wave-mcp/bin/pip install wave-mcp`, pin MPD_DSH_WAVE_MCP_BIN) or pipx; TraceWeave → SEPARATE venv (~/.venvs/traceweave) — never share with wave-mcp (MCP SDK v2 vs mcp==1.27.0 conflict, t1 evidence) — then point MPD_DSH_TRACEWEAVE_BIN at <venv>/bin/traceweave-mcp. NEVER bare system pip. Both degrade gracefully when absent (see DP-9).\n- session-dir policy = DP-8; handshake/wiring notes go into docs/rtl-verif-guide (t9).\n\n═══ §6 RISK TIERS + P0/P1 ═══\nR1 LOW: skill refs, templates, docs, deferred-list records.\nR2 MEDIUM: mpd-verif OSS lane (venv iron rule, compile/sim/regress), VENDOR_LOCK re-lock, MCP rows, UVM gating logic (untestable-for-real w/o VCS → QA = refusal paths + arg-construction unit tests), LSP overlay rebuild (guarded).\nR3 HIGH: real VCS runs (no VCS on QA machine → P0 ships refusal-path + docs; real smoke is owner-side, documented), TraceWeave EDA lane end-to-end (no VERDI/NOVAS here), LSP rebuild env dependency (MPD_UPSTREAM_ROOT + bun cache — present on this machine, must be documented for future builds).\nP0 (must ship): LSP builtins (overlay+rebuild+re-lock+skill refs) · mpd-verif core 6 tools with iron rule + gating · UVM VCS-lane orchestration (refusal-tested) · wave-mcp+traceweave rows + wiring notes · bilingual docs skeleton (t9) · full QA gate evidence (t7).\nP1 (only after P0 clean): VCS coverage merge automation polish · TraceWeave EDA deep wiring · verible.filelist auto-gen helper · .slang/server.json template generator · regress parallelization · zh-CN translations of lsp refs if owner wants.\n\n═══ §7 ENGINEERING-FLOW RECOMMENDATIONS — DRAFT OUTLINE ONLY (NOT settled; owner consultation required) ═══\n(1) lint-in-loop (LSP diagnostics + mpd_verif_compile pre-commit) · (2) cocotb-first OSS TB (one @cocotb.test() per case, results.xml→CI) · (3) UVM only on VCS + escalation criteria cocotb→UVM · (4) waveform review gate (FST via wave-mcp/%surfer after each regress; fix-before-merge discussion) · (5) golden RTL flow: C-model → verilog-generator-style templates → lint → sim → regress → wave review → merge · (6) env hygiene (MPD_DSH_*, per-project venv, VCS license env) · (7) regression hygiene (seed rule, per-case work dirs, results.json archive). t9 renders these in docs/rtl-verif-guide under a flagged \"建议 (DRAFT, pending owner sign-off)\" section — treat NONE as normative until owner confirms (DP-10).\n\n═══ DECISION POINTS (captain → owner) ═══\n- DP-1 LSP form: approve Option A (builtin overlay + rebuild + re-lock; ~2-4 h) as primary, Option B as documented escape hatch? (Reject A → B-only fallback; HDL then NOT auto-resolved per extension and t7 acceptance changes.)\n- DP-2 LSP ids/extensions: \"verible\"→[.v,.vh], \"slang-server\"→[.sv,.svh] (no overlap). Alternative: verible also on .sv at lower priority / different ids.\n- DP-3 Skill-ref language: EN-only (consistent w/ 18 existing refs; bilingual cover in docs/) vs bilingual refs too.\n- DP-4 Tool surface: approve exactly 6 tools (venv/backends/compile/sim/uvm/regress; regress folds in the report). No front-end; nothing else.\n- DP-5 Venv location: default <workspace>/.venv-rtl per project + MPD_DSH_VERIF_VENV override (recommended) vs one shared tool venv.\n- DP-6 Cocotb runner: generated runner.py via cocotb.runner API — no make dependency (recommended) vs generated Makefile (cocotb canonical docs flow); both pin venv python; cocotb>=2.0.\n- DP-7 Gates: hard refusal both directions (vcs+cocotb REFUSE; non-vcs+uvm REFUSE) — confirm hard vs warning.\n- DP-8 wave-mcp session dir: default $DSH_HOME/wave-mcp via MPD_DSH_WAVE_MCP_SESSION override, vs ~/.mpd/…, vs per-workspace (NOT possible in one boot-level row).\n- DP-9 Boot degradation: confirm \"row present, gracefully degrade when binary absent\" as the documented norm; QA item P0-7 verifies dsh-mcp-client tolerates missing command (unverified assumption — see below). Fallback: ship rows disabled-by-default + docs to enable.\n- DP-10 Recommendations: confirm DRAFT-flagged placement in docs pending owner sign-off.\n- DP-11 P0/P1 split: confirm P0 scope; VCS real-run validation is owner-side (no VCS in our QA env).\n\n═══ FILE-TOUCH MAP (for engineers — NOT edited in this design phase) ═══\nt3: packages/mpd-mcp-lsp/overlay/lsp/* ; scripts/build-mcp.mjs ; rebuild dist/cli.js + BUILD.lock ; VENDOR_LOCK.json re-lock ; skills/lsp-setup/references/{verilog,systemverilog}/README.md ; skills/lsp-setup/SKILL.md ; packages/mpd-mcp-lsp/templates/rtl-lsp-client.json ; rtl-codestyle skill templates (verilog-generator style).\nt4: packages/mpd-verif-plugin/** ; bundle row ; dsh-qa case script+SKILL row.\nt5: skills/rtl-verif/** (cocotb TB + UVM skeletons + regression workspace scaffold).\nt9: cordis.patch.yml MCP rows (mcp-wave-mcp, mcp-traceweave) ; docs/rtl-verif-guide.md + .zh-CN.md (+ zh link rule) ; deferred to-do list ; recommendations section.\nt7 acceptance sweep per AGENTS.md §4 (isolated DSH_HOME only): vendor gate after re-lock · per-package bun test + typecheck · test:qa --self-test · real roundtrips (LSP: temp-downloaded verible/slang binaries on PATH → real diagnostics on .v/.sv; verif: compile bad-good .v, venv iron-rule refusal + create + sim adder w/ results.xml + FST, backends probe incl. vcs-absent, regress 2-case, refusal paths for vcs+cocotb/non-vcs+uvm, system-python still cocotb-free) · boot --dump-config shows new rows · evidence under evidence/rtl-{lsp,verif}/.\n\nASSUMPTIONS (unverified, QA will settle): dsh-mcp-client tolerates a not-installed MCP command at boot (P0-7 probe; fallback shipped-disabled) · bun cache holds js-yaml/jsonc-parser/zod for the lsp rebuild (BUILD.lock confirms at build time) · cocotb.runner API fidelity at 2.0.x (t7 real run) · icarus FST flag name (t4/t7) · LSP_TOOLS_MCP_USER_CONFIG h